= attitudes towards logic =
====== short ======

====== related to ======
-[[local:zz.texts/williamson1986-theContingentAPrioriHasItAnythingToDoWithIndexicals.pdf]]

= main =
Traditional options include:
- fundamental metaphysical structure grasped by the reasoning mind.
- analytic truths made true by the meaning of the terms <q>or</q> <q>and</q>


My view is that they are contingent but self evident truths in the sense that in
each world they are believed/considered/uttered they are true.

In the worlds in which they are not uttered/considered/
Not true in the sense that their negation is true, but in the sense that they do
not feature in true theories of those simple worlds.
